WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.660
Oh, Ben Affleck, how we love you for what
you've given to the Batman role.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.560
Now, it's time for you to leave.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.450
Sure, Affleck is the biggest star in the DC
Extended Universe of films.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.009
But is he actually hurting both the franchise
and his own career?

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:17.900
Here's a look at some of the real reasons
Ben Affleck needs to get out of his Batman

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.699
contract.

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:21.259
Critical bombs

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:25.720
Let's face it: Batman versus Superman and
Justice League's critical receptions probably

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.479
aren't helping Ben Affleck's overall artistic
morale, what with him waking up every morning

00:00:30.479 --> 00:00:33.010
to green splatters on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:38.170
Even Suicide Squad, in which he only made
a cameo appearance, tanked harshly with critics.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.910
Considering Affleck spent years trying to
rebuild his reputation as a serious actor

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.681
after Daredevil flopped, he's just not doing
himself any favors by going down with the

00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:48.780
DCEU ship.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.030
An uncomfortable fit

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.390
Affleck's version of Batman is possibly the
grimmest one yet.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:58.489
But is that a reflection of the overall dourness
of the DCEU?

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:01.519
Or is it a reflection of how Affleck feels
about playing the role?

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.470
Either way, fans and critics alike agree that
his work is suffering.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.479
For instance, The Guardian's review of Justice
League said

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:13.799
"Ben Affleck is unrelaxed and ill-at-ease
in the role of Batman/Bruce, unconvincing

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:17.570
in both the bat armour and the three-piece
suit of the wealthy plutocrat.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.899
[…] Affleck spreads a pall of dullness over
the film."

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:22.610
Polygon agreed, writing,

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.350
"Affleck's performance is barely passable."

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.610
Whether the cause is personal or professional,
it's clear to everyone that Affleck's heart

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.470
just isn't in it.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.600
And exhibit A is...

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.420
The Sad Affleck meme

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.320
When Sad Keanu became a meme, Keanu Reeves
got a kick out of making fun of himself.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.130
But even Sad Keanu feels bad for what happened
to Ben Affleck after his Batman versus Superman

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:48.710
interview with co-star Henry Cavill went infamously
off the rails.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:53.159
"It taught me not to do interviews Henry Cavill
where I don't say anything and they can lay

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.969
Simon and Garfunkel tracks over it, that's
one thing I learned."

00:01:56.969 --> 00:02:00.619
If there's one thing we know, it's that the
internet never forgets a good meme, and now

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:05.079
there's a whole generation, who knows Affleck
mainly as "that sad meme guy."

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:09.570
For the sake of his mental health if nothing
else, maybe he should get out before any more

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.540
memes come along.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.120
Creative differences

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.390
When Affleck first signed on to play Batman,
it was a really big deal, and the Oscar winner

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:21.300
was set to direct, write, and star in a Batman
solo film.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.450
It seemed as if he had been given total control,
and he was stoked.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:28.030
"I wanted to be in one of these movies that
was ballsy and that had something to say,

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:28.820
you know?

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.520
And I wanted to do a movie that my kids would
think was cool."

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.800
But slowly, it became apparent that Affleck
and Warner Brothers were experiencing those

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.090
dreaded "creative differences."

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.010
First Affleck dropped out as director, then
he dropped out as writer.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.790
And with new director Matt Reeves reportedly
pushing the film in a new direction, rumors

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.490
began that Affleck would drop out as the star
too!

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:55.040
Given the repeated votes of no confidence
shown him by the studio, why would Affleck

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.110
even want to stay as a puppet in someone else's
show?

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.120
A dignified exit

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.420
Speaking of director Matt Reeves, reports
have surfaced claiming that he wants to replace

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.720
Affleck as the man in the bat suit.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.830
And there are plenty of stars who seem far
more eager than Affleck to don the cowl.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.740
For example, Reeves apparently has his eye
on Jake Gyllenhaal, while Jon Hamm is also

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.880
reportedly gunning hard for the role.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.060
"Lucky lad!"

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.140
"Feelin' lucky?"

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.120
Given how disappointing all the DCEU films
have been so far, we're not sure Hamm or Gyllenhaal

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.310
could do any better than Affleck has done.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.240
But considering he no longer seems to be wanted,
Affleck could spare himself a lot of embarrassment

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.060
if he quit before Warner Brothers has the
chance to fire him.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.290
The grass is greener

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.150
Considering Affleck has a proven track record
as a creative force, winning the Best Picture

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:48.010
Oscar for Argo in 2013 and the Best Original
Screenplay Oscar for Good Will Hunting in

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.570
1998, there are plenty of opportunities for
Affleck in Hollywood that don't involve being

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:56.200
a punching bag for fans, critics, his own
studio, and Superman.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:01.700
Heck, before filming Batman versus Superman,
Affleck was on a roll, coming off of an acclaimed

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.780
performance in the 2014 hit Gone Girl.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.290
That's the star that fans were hoping to see
in the DCEU.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.860
And it's the star fans are now hoping they
can see pretty much anywhere else, because

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.650
since stepping into the role of Batman, Affleck
has been in a deep creative funk.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.209
Given that Affleck certainly doesn't need
the money, and given that even his closest

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:24.080
family and friends are lobbying for him to
leave, here's hoping that he gets out of his

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.669
Batman contract sooner rather than later.

00:04:26.669 --> 00:04:30.710
It wouldn't just make fans happy - it would
make both Warner Brothers and Affleck much

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.039
happier too.

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:35.690
And that's the kind of win rate even Batman
would be envious of.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.000
Thanks for watching!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.689
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:39.689 --> 00:04:42.129
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

